# Example Caddy snippet — adapt host/path; do not commit real tokens.
#
# Option A: Bearer via forward auth / header check (preferred if you already
# use the same pattern for Hindsight MCP).
#
# Option B: basic auth in front of the dashboard.

# handle_path /hinddian/* {
#     basicauth {
#         # caddy hash-password — put hash here, not plaintext
#         wanwan JDJh...replace_me
#     }
#     reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8787
# }

# If using API AUTH_TOKEN instead of basic auth, clients send:
#   Authorization: Bearer <token>
# and Caddy can just reverse_proxy without exposing the port publicly.
